Description: Builds multimodal transport networks from 'OpenStreetMap'
    extracts, 'GTFS' feeds and, optionally, an elevation raster, and routes
    on them by walking, cycling, driving and public transport. Computes
    travel-time matrices, accessibility to opportunities, isochrones,
    detailed itineraries and trip options that trade off travel time, fare,
    transfers and walking. Supports fare structures, slope-aware walking and
    cycling, and scenarios of car speeds and cycling stress applied per call
    without rebuilding the network. The routing engine is written in 'Rust':
    it runs inside the R session with no 'Java' runtime, keeps the network
    in memory, uses all cores, and is shared with the 'Python' and
    'JavaScript' packages of the same name. The methods follow Conveyal's
    'R5' routing engine, Conway, Byrd and van der Linden (2017)
    <doi:10.3141/2653-06>, with the round-based public transport routing of
    Delling, Pajor and Werneck (2015) <doi:10.1287/trsc.2014.0534>, the
    travel-time percentiles of Conway, Byrd and van Eggermond (2018)
    <doi:10.5198/jtlu.2018.1074>, the fare-constrained routing of Conway
    and Stewart (2019) <doi:10.1080/13658816.2019.1605075> and the
    contraction hierarchies of Geisberger, Sanders, Schultes and Vetter
    (2012) <doi:10.1287/trsc.1110.0401>.
